    "summary": "Adire sample of dyeing techniques. The cloth is formed of two lengths of imported European machine calico cotton sheeting, folded together. The cloth has been tied using raffia palm fibre and stitch-dyed in indigo, but has been only in part unstitched. At the end are small circles produced by tying around small objects. In the middle is a pattern of dashes (short lines).",
